{"id":"mulesg09-befjsd","at":"2026-09-28T15:35:11.625Z","listId":"main","label":"Wave 7 — Gardenize and Dryad in","author":"user","rationale":"Gardenize: charge counter per creature dying (tokens DO die, CR 111.7, unlike descend) and the counters are permanent, so the mana RECURS every first main phase - a ratchet not a ritual. Doubling Season doubles the charge counters (verified oracle: 'twice that many of those counters'). It is an enchantment, so it is the only mana source here a creature wipe cannot answer. Dryad of the Ilysian Grove: a SECOND extra land drop that STACKS with Oracle of Mul Daya for three lands a turn, feeding four landfall payoffs (Tireless Provisioner, Tireless Tracker, Scute Swarm self-copy at six lands, Avenger of Zendikar); its second line makes Gaea's Cradle tap for any colour. OUT: Orcrist, Goblin-cleaver - pilot playtested it, it worked, but it needs to go on a non-commander body and equipping Chatterfang raised his threat profile; the deck's four kill routes need no combat step. OUT: Chitterspitter - pilot never cast it once across games; three mana for +1/+1 next turn lost every comparison to three mana of immediate value. Curve-neutral by construction: three MV3 out, two MV3 in, avg MV and MV<=2 unchanged. Ninja Pizza KEPT at pilot's direction - it converts idle Foods into mana.","entries":[{"op":"add","name":"Gardenize","section":"Ramp & Mana","replaces":"Orcrist, Goblin-cleaver"},{"op":"add","name":"Dryad of the Ilysian Grove","section":"Ramp & Mana","replaces":"Chitterspitter"},{"op":"remove","name":"Orcrist, Goblin-cleaver"},{"op":"remove","name":"Chitterspitter"}],"snapshot":"versions/2026-09-28-1535-main-wave-7-gardenize-and-dryad-in.json","before":{"size":{"total":100,"target":100,"lands":36,"nonland":64,"commanders":1},"curve":{"avgMv":2.83,"avgMvNonZero":2.83,"histogram":[{"mv":"0","creature":0,"noncreature":0},{"mv":"1","creature":5,"noncreature":4},{"mv":"2","creature":7,"noncreature":11},{"mv":"3","creature":12,"noncreatur