{"id":"mulld5zz-fl2www","at":"2026-09-28T18:39:16.127Z","listId":"main","label":"Starscape Cleric in for Viscera Seer","author":"user","rationale":"Starscape Cleric is converter #3 against FIFTEEN measured lifegain sources in the list (High Market, Ninja Pizza, Tireless Provisioner, Moldervine Reclamation, Meathook Massacre, Peregrin Took, Tippy-Toe, Ravenous Squirrel, Bastion, Blood Artist, Cauldron of Essence, Nadier's Nightblade, Prosperous Innkeeper, Valley Rotcaller, Zulaport) against only TWO converters (Dina, Vito). A converter multiplies all fifteen; more fuel would only add a sixteenth thing for two cards to multiply. 'Each opponent loses 1 life' is the right shape here because every one of those fifteen gains exactly 1 life at a time - per the many-small-events rule, that beats Vito's single-target 'that much' on this profile, 3x over in a four-player pod. Offspring {2}{B} makes a 1/1 token COPY that is also a converter, and because the word is 'create' Chatterfang adds a Squirrel and Mirkwood Bats pings for both. OUT Viscera Seer: the one genuinely surplus card in the list - Woe Strider strictly dominates it (free sacrifice AND scry 1 AND brings a Goat AND escapes from the graveyard), and five free outlets remain plus Chatterfang, three lands and three spells when you only ever need one in play. Curve: MV<=2 stays 27, MV<=3 stays 49, avg MV 2.83 -> 2.84.","entries":[{"op":"add","name":"Starscape Cleric","section":"Drain Payoffs","replaces":"Viscera Seer"},{"op":"remove","name":"Viscera Seer"}],"snapshot":"versions/2026-09-28-1839-main-starscape-cleric-in-for-viscera-seer.json","before":{"size":{"total":100,"target":100,"lands":36,"nonland":64,"commanders":1},"curve":{"avgMv":2.83,"avgMvNonZero":2.83,"histogram":[{"mv":"0","creature":0,"noncreature":0},{"mv":"1","creature":5,"noncreature":4},{"mv":"2","creature":7,"noncreature":11},{"mv":"3","creature":13,"noncreature":9},{"mv":"4","creature":8,"noncreature":2},{"mv":"5","creature":0,"noncreature":3},{"mv"